WEBVTT

00:00.270 --> 00:02.100
Instructor: So far, we've used git tag

00:02.100 --> 00:05.910
to generate a tag that refers to the current head commit.

00:05.910 --> 00:08.640
But we can also go back and tag earlier commits

00:08.640 --> 00:11.340
by using the commit hash.

00:11.340 --> 00:15.000
So, if I do a git log --oneline on this react repo,

00:15.000 --> 00:16.770
let's take some earlier commit,

00:16.770 --> 00:18.513
really, any earlier commit.

00:19.830 --> 00:23.040
Let's, I don't know, there's so many to choose from.

00:23.040 --> 00:24.750
Let's take one of them.

00:24.750 --> 00:27.840
How about right here, remove JSX plugin.

00:27.840 --> 00:30.630
If you're following along, just pick any commit, really.

00:30.630 --> 00:32.520
Actually, you know what? I regret this.

00:32.520 --> 00:35.970
I think something closer to the top will be easier to see.

00:35.970 --> 00:37.770
Okay, how about this one right here?

00:38.790 --> 00:40.350
Request to update email.

00:40.350 --> 00:41.490
So whatever,

00:41.490 --> 00:43.860
on your git log, whatever you see,

00:43.860 --> 00:45.720
just go back a couple of commits,

00:45.720 --> 00:49.590
maybe five, 10 commits earlier before any tags we've created

00:49.590 --> 00:52.020
and copy one of those hashes.

00:52.020 --> 00:55.260
So right now, we don't see a tag here but I can add one

00:55.260 --> 00:56.640
if I do git tag,

00:56.640 --> 00:58.230
and then a tag name,

00:58.230 --> 01:00.030
and then the commit hash.

01:00.030 --> 01:01.830
And this can be lightweight or annotated.

01:01.830 --> 01:03.720
I use -a for annotated.

01:03.720 --> 01:06.090
To make it simple, I'll use lightweight.

01:06.090 --> 01:09.630
So, git tag and then tag name,

01:09.630 --> 01:12.183
let's just do something, I don't know, mytag,

01:12.183 --> 01:13.590
just to demonstrate, right?

01:13.590 --> 01:15.630
It doesn't have to be a version number.

01:15.630 --> 01:17.590
And then, I'll put the commit hash

01:18.780 --> 01:20.490
and we don't really see much.

01:20.490 --> 01:21.783
If I do git tag,

01:23.070 --> 01:24.930
we'll see my tag in there.

01:24.930 --> 01:26.040
There it is.

01:26.040 --> 01:30.000
But also, if I do git log --oneline or just git log,

01:30.000 --> 01:30.833
there it is.

01:30.833 --> 01:33.960
We tagged that previous, that earlier commit.

01:33.960 --> 01:36.160
That's really all I wanted to show you here.
